-- title:
--   Lifting a complete-intersection presentation from the residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring which is complete (and separated) with respect to its maximal-ideal adic topology, with residue field $k = \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}$, and let $T$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Assume that the special fibre admits a presentation with equally many variables and relations: there exist $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and a family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to k[[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n]]$ of multivariate formal power series over $k$ such that the quotient of $k[[X_i]]$ by the ideal generated by the range of $g$ is isomorphic, as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, to $T/\mathfrak{m}T$, where $\mathfrak{m}T$ denotes the image ideal $(\mathfrak{m})\cdot T$ obtained by pushing $\mathfrak{m}$ forward along $\mathcal{O} \to T$. The conclusion is that the same shape of presentation exists over $\mathcal{O}$ itself: there exist $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathcal{O}[[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,m]]$ together with an isomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $\mathcal{O}[[X_i]]/(\mathrm{range}\,f) \cong T$. The number of variables produced is existentially quantified, so the statement does not record that one may take $m = n$.
--
--   This is the complete-intersection lifting step of the commutative algebra behind the Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion (Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, Prop. 5.29): a finite flat algebra over a complete Noetherian local ring whose fibre over the residue field is a complete intersection is itself presented by equally many power series relations as variables. It is used in [`AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le`](thm.html#AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le), where the Hecke-type algebra $T$ is shown to be a complete intersection.
